  "usage": "Give items as rows {name, room: pcb|embedded|cad|mobile|web|analyze, deps: comma-separated names it depends on}, changed as comma-separated item names and maxHops (0 = unlimited). It returns the affected items with hop count, weight (0.5^(hops-1)) and the dependency path that reaches them, a per-room table and chart, an overall score and level (low/medium/high), warnings for unknown names and dependency cycles, and a per-room review checklist. Use it before an engineering change to see which teams must re-check their work.",
  "sources": [
    "Bohner & Arnold, Software Change Impact Analysis, IEEE Computer Society Press 1996 (impact set as transitive dependants)",
    "Tarjan, 'Depth-first search and linear graph algorithms', SIAM J. Computing 1972 (cycle detection)",
    "Rule of thumb: halving weight per hop and the low/medium/high thresholds"
  ]
}
